No, pieere is right.. Fro the Grammar, 3.9:

Most Lojban words are stressed on the next-to-the-last, or penultimate,
syllable. In counting syllables, however, syllables whose vowel is ``y''
or which contain a syllabic consonant (``l'', ``m'', ``n'', or ``r'')
are never counted. (The Lojban term for penultimate stress is ``da'amoi
terbasna''.) Similarly, syllables created solely by adding a buffer
vowel, such as [I], are not counted.=20

=20

  And yes, I did realize after I read my own message that I meant to say
"only y", but I didn't think it important enough to correct.

        gejyspa

